    "title": "What time is Tigers game vs Boston Red Sox today?",
    "text": "Updated April 20, 2026, 7:16 a.m. ETGrab some Dunkin’ (or a Sam Adams, we guess), cook up a bowl of chowder and get ready for a morning IN BAW-STUN.Yes, just a few hours after the Detroit Tigers' game in Boston on Sunday, April 19, was shipped off to ... three hours later, thanks to weather concerns, the Motor City's crew will look to heist the four-game series with an 11:10 a.m. start.Why?Well, it’s a double-dip in Massachusetts for Patriots’ Day, with the Boston Marathon starting bright and early (and televised beginning at 9 a.m. on ESPN2), followed by the Tigers’ game against the Boston Red Sox at 11:10 a.m. on Detroit SportsNet (or MLB Network, where available).After that, with all afternoon to yourself? Maybe cue up “The Departed” or “Good Will Hunting,” your call.Here's what we know about the Tigers' finale at Fenway Park (in which the home squad will likely be wearing their yellows-and-blues for the third straight game) before they come home for three games against the Milwaukee Brewers (don't tell them about the Sam Adams, though).What time is the Tigers game today?Time: 11:10 a.m. ET.Date: Monday, April 20.Location: Fenway Park, Boston.Box score.[No Boston visit for JV, as rehabbing righty cancels travel plans ]What channel is Tigers vs Red Sox on today?TV channel: Detroit SportsNet.First pitch: 11:10 a.m. ET.Streaming: Fubo.Radio: WXYT-FM (97.1).Monday's game can be watched on Detroit SportsNet, which also offers streaming, or online via Fubo.Celebrate 125 years of Tigers history with our book!Tigers vs Red Sox pitching matchup on SundayDET: RHP Jack Flaherty (0-1, 4.05 ERA)BOS: RHP Sonny Gray (2-1, 4.43 ERA).Flaherty is coming off a gem last week in which he struck out seven against the Kansas City Royals while allowing just two hits (and three walks) in six innings.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
